// Expected: a0 at one session and a1 at two.
//
// Alice signs a fresh message and hands it to Bob on an open leg; Bob
// verifies it and does nothing else. At one session there is no second
// flight to hand him, so the query holds.
//
// At two the attacker takes Alice's other run's pair off the wire and gives
// it to this Bob, whose check passes because the signature is Alice's own.
// Nothing is forged: Alice sent that pair once and both of her Bobs accept
// it, so agreement is not injective. Bob contributes nothing to the message
// before accepting it, so the verdict carries
// Subtype::ReplayableFirstFlight rather than DuplicateAcceptance.
//
// This is the smallest shape of that duplicate, and the baseline
// duplicate_acceptance_partial_guarded_forward.vp has to reproduce.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	knows private sk
	pk = PUBKEY(sk)
	generates m
	s = SIGN(sk, m)
]

Alice -> Bob: [pk], m, s

principal Bob[
	_ = SIGNVERIF(pk, m, s)?
]

queries[
	authentication? Alice -> Bob: m
]
